{"event_type":"review","id":"ab82e0487d4db85e2ba263b65ee0944ee9fad1d2f160afe9a00179eebaf87c00","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T09:55:44Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/767cd3f7d9096c688af0982345328b5d4952ddddc7e065b6831c46edfef35adf","sha256":"767cd3f7d9096c688af0982345328b5d4952ddddc7e065b6831c46edfef35adf"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/16bdeb7370bc6655c4bf3149dfff952861cda96deef8c9ba902fc38310cecc9a","sha256":"16bdeb7370bc6655c4bf3149dfff952861cda96deef8c9ba902fc38310cecc9a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b304353b1502d1c2e0f8b0ed2bf155ef971683f0d5b09ce21dbf2abe7cce2428","sha256":"b304353b1502d1c2e0f8b0ed2bf155ef971683f0d5b09ce21dbf2abe7cce2428"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/84846d2a5764b5f852212adbab42fd86eeb5e3810ac9e56b97876ffce0b419b3","sha256":"84846d2a5764b5f852212adbab42fd86eeb5e3810ac9e56b97876ffce0b419b3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cce65d54ea9a7aaba29c0adeb5eeecd8948d2a960c877c9a83aa91e7f4662aeb","sha256":"cce65d54ea9a7aaba29c0adeb5eeecd8948d2a960c877c9a83aa91e7f4662aeb"}],"attempt_id":"d78b9a3bcb3814ac16f26456a36e6a53ccce83ae69dddd98b55fed5571829be8:0:1","base":"e1a0bbb91ba4ab3fce6f041704fed83a0c1697bd","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b62a9f851c394e1dc3079d82f992f424189f2a5c","body":"**After a crash, an existing inbox job file is kept even when its `repair_base` no longer matches the new record. This blocks `harvest` on every tick.**\n\n`enqueue` writes the job files, but it does not call `save_queue`; the caller saves the queue later. Suppose the process crashes after `atomic(path, job)` (`repair_tick.py:99`) but before the queue is saved. On the next run, `enqueue` builds a new `record`. For non-PR items, `base` is computed again from `origin/merge-queue` (line 83), and that ref may have moved. Line 98 then keeps the old job file, which still has the old `repair_base`.\n\nThe worker repairs from the old base. In `harvest`, line 138 compares `result['repair_base']` against the new `record['base']`. They differ, so it raises `ValueError('repair predecessor mismatch')`. The exception leaves `harvest` uncaught on every tick, so this run never recovers without manual work.\n\nFix: if the job file already exists, either reuse its `repair_base` for the new `record`, or refuse when the stored binding differs:\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         path = c.STATE / 'repair/inbox' / (job_id + '.json')\n-        if not path.exists():\n+        if path.exists():\n+            prior_job = json.loads(path.read_text())\n+            if prior_job.get('repair_base') != base or prior_job.get('finding') != finding:\n+                item['last_error'] = 'stale inbox job ' + job_id + ' from interrupted enqueue; needs human'\n+                return False\n+        else:\n             atomic(path, job)\n```\n</details>","id":"57fcc121e73a71eac918b936043ade44ca1c328801282bd183bc6717a68b5215","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"After a crash, an existing inbox job file is kept even when its `repairbase` no longer matches the new record. This blocks `harvest` on every tick."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b62a9f851c394e1dc3079d82f992f424189f2a5c","body":"**Reject an inbox job whose repair base changed.**\n\nA crash after `atomic(path, job)` and before the queue save can leave the old job file without its queue record. On the next tick, `job_id` still uses `run_id` and the finding index, so a changed `origin/merge-queue` base reuses the same path. `enqueue` keeps the old file but records the new base.\n\nIf that job returns `FIXED`, `harvest` raises `ValueError('repair predecessor mismatch')` before updating the record. `crq.py` catches the exception and saves an error, but it does not mark the record resolved. The same repair record can therefore fail again on later ticks.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         path = c.STATE / 'repair/inbox' / (job_id + '.json')\n-        if not path.exists():\n+        if path.exists():\n+            prior_job = json.loads(path.read_text())\n+            if prior_job.get('repair_base') != base or prior_job.get('finding') != finding:\n+                item['last_error'] = 'stale inbox job ' + job_id + ' from interrupted enqueue; needs human'\n+                return False\n+        else:\n             atomic(path, job)\n```\n\n</details>","id":"09b67881ba74029c4ecccf7a967d1a4aac9612e7379a8657fe5e7809fee427a4","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject an inbox job whose repair base changed."}],"head":"1b6e83310df347d0e5d07dacdbe63aa605416504","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"a684c71fc18b709bc2faa7258a2139eb6494abf4","intervals":[[1,467]],"path":"apps/crq-python/merged_reconcile.py"},{"blob":"b62a9f851c394e1dc3079d82f992f424189f2a5c","intervals":[[1,413]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py"},{"blob":"c18a2b091d7d309e7b593ef06086b5933c0c26a2","intervals":[[1,484]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_snapshot.py"},{"blob":"50595b6ab8462f27e62304f73c63cf39434c2c89","intervals":[[1,306]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_transport.py"},{"blob":"e9a10fbf11b2bb52864d24c5237b557d5f70737f","intervals":[[1,259]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_accounting.py"},{"blob":"cc81e6833280a4159e3a1ea96331950e4408bdde","intervals":[[1,316]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_runtime.py"},{"blob":"ff7e5829e1980621dd14601919b02328aa9e2187","intervals":[[1,423]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_promotion_retry.py"},{"blob":"49407c5769512e79dce0c4